  "response": {
    "text": "Use this procedure to load fresh fuel into reactor cell `RX-3A`. This procedure does not affect backup cell `RX-3B`.\n\n1. Verify that license `NRC-8801` is current.\n2. Confirm that cell `RX-3A` coolant flow shows **Normal**.\n3. Confirm that the control rods indicate `full-insertion`.\n4. Execute `hyperctl status RX-3A`.\n5. Continue only if the output shows `temp=ambient pressure=nominal`.\n\nWARNING: The next step initiates irreversible fuel loading into cell `RX-3A`. Emergency shutdown after loading requires regulatory approval.\n\n6. Execute `hyperctl load-fuel RX-3A --license NRC-8801`.\n7. After loading completes, run `hyperctl verify RX-3A`.\n8. Confirm that the output is `fuel=loaded rods=inserted`.",
